        "title": "Newborn Breastfeeding Frequency - La Leche League International",
        "url": "https://llli.org/breastfeeding-info/frequency-feeding-frequently-asked-questions-faqs/",
        "description": "This recommendation is well supported by a great deal of research evidence[vii] as well as by the American Academy of Family Physicians[viii] (AAFP) and the American Academy of Pediatrics[ix] (AAP) in the US, and the National Institute for Health and Care Excellence (NICE) in the UK.[x] In addition, research shows that successful lactation depends on 8 or more nursings in 24 hours, both day and night, throughout the first month;1 by establishing this pattern during the first few days, you will get breastfeeding off to a good start.",
