      {
        "title": "Essential Guide: Breastfeeding at 3-6 Weeks Postpartum - Physician Guide to Breastfeeding",
        "url": "https://physicianguidetobreastfeeding.org/breastfeeding-basics/next-steps-3-6-weeks/",
        "description": "However, the 4-6 week period can be difficult in the afternoon and evenings, when babies seem inconsolable. They may want to “cluster feed” as they search for comfort, but are sometimes unable to find relief — even at the breast. This is a time, if breastfeeding is well established, to introduce a pacifier and take a baby outside for fresh air to calm them.",
