      },
      {
        "title": "Establishing and maintaining milk supply when baby is not breastfeeding - KellyMom.com",
        "url": "https://kellymom.com/ages/newborn/nb-challenges/maintainsupply-pump/",
        "description": "If you have twins or higher order multiples, <strong>aim for pumping 800-950 mL (27-32 oz) by 14 days postpartum</strong>. It’s useful to evaluate mom’s 24 hour pumping output at 10 days. If supply is borderline (350-500 ml / 11-17 oz) or low (less than 350 ml / 11 oz), then galactagogues (prescription ...",
