        "position": 5
      },
      {
        "title": "Breastfeeding at 2 Weeks A Counseling Guide for Health Care Professionals",
        "url": "https://www.kdhe.ks.gov/DocumentCenter/View/11878/Breastfeeding-at-2-weeks-PDF",
        "description": "days. Frequent nursing will increase mother’s · milk supply to meet baby’s new needs. Avoid pacifiers and bottles for the first 3-4 · weeks. Encourage mothers to wait until their milk · supply is established before introducing · pacifiers or bottles. Frequent use of pacifiers · makes it hard for mothers to tell when baby is · hungry. Early use of bottles decreases · mother’s milk supply and leads to early · weaning. Breastfeeding ...",
        "position": 6
